Controlled-300 project licensing
Copyright (c) 2026 Rahul Maddineni

This project uses separate licences for original software and original research
material. These grants apply only to rights held by Rahul Maddineni and do not
override existing third-party licences or notices.

1. Original software

Original evaluation-framework code, dashboard code, scripts, tests, notebook
code cells and configuration files are licensed under the MIT License. The
full licence text is in LICENSES/MIT.txt.

2. Original research material

Original narrative documentation, notebook explanatory text, reports, original
research figures and research-result compilations are licensed under Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), to the extent that the author
holds the relevant copyright or database rights. See LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.
No exclusive rights are claimed over facts or public-domain material.

3. Third-party exclusions

The grants above do not relicense source paintings or their digital images,
third-party artwork or visual elements, third-party code, dependencies, model
weights, checkpoints, training data, or externally sourced material. Existing
rights statements and licence conditions continue to apply. Third-party
elements embedded in a figure, report or dashboard screenshot are excluded
from the licence grant for the author's original contribution.

Painting-source rights and provenance are recorded in
data/raw/metadata/metadata_300.csv and
outputs/01_dataset_verification/data/artworks.csv. Model-specific disclosures
are recorded in the model cards and docs/model_audit_notes.md. These records
are provenance aids, not a comprehensive legal clearance or a substitute for
the applicable upstream terms. A software licence does not establish the
licence for its model weights or training data.

Redistribution packages must retain applicable upstream notices and identify
third-party material. Content whose redistribution terms have not been
established must not be treated as cleared by this project-level notice.

4. Attribution

Credit original research material to Rahul Maddineni, University of Applied
Sciences Technikum Wien, and identify the project as:
Trustworthy Evaluation Frameworks for AI-Assisted Painting Restoration:
Controlled-300 Research Artifacts.

The affiliation is supplied for attribution and does not imply institutional
endorsement. Citation metadata and any future DOI complement, rather than
replace, the applicable licence conditions.
